{"step_index":6841,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-24T14:41:34Z","thinking":"Determining the default model for the local API call is necessary; it defaults to a specific model if not configured. Preparing the request body involves constructing a message array that includes system instructions and user input formatted as JSON. The JSON serialization must ensure proper encoding to handle various characters.\n\n\nConstructing the API endpoint URL requires checking for existing suffixes and appending \"chat/completions\" if necessary, with a preference for a \"v1\" path when possible. Authentication utilizes an API key, retrieved from configuration. The HTTP request includes the URL, headers with authorization and content type, the JSON body, and a timeout to handle potential latency. Error handling involves specific error messages and logging based on HTTP status codes or connection failures.\n\n\nInitial response parsing focuses on retrieving the content from the API's choice. Potential error strings are checked early to avoid incorrect JSON parsing. Robust JSON extraction is attempted using markdown code blocks, then outermost curly braces, and finally outermost square brackets to handle varied response formats. If the content isn't parsable or contains an error, the exception is logged.\n\n\nResponse data is processed based on type, checking for a list or dictionary structure within the parsed output to extract results. A default 'no_match' status is applied if a case ID isn't found in the response. Errors are logged to a file, including details such as timestamp, error type, URL, model, case IDs, and the raw response for debugging.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Add robust JSON extraction and provider_errors.log diagnostics to _call_local_api","EndLine":596,"Instruction":"Replace _call_local_api with robust JSON extraction and logging","ReplacementContent":"    def _call_local_api(self, inputs: dict) -> list[dict]:\n        model = getattr(self.config, 'local_model', 'gpt-4o')\n        \n        body = {\n            \"model\": model,\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": SYSTEM_PROMPT},\n                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": json.dumps(inputs, ensure_ascii=False)}\n            ]\n        }\n\n        raw_url = getattr(self.config, 'local_api_url', \"http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1/chat/completions\")\n        url = str(raw_url).strip().rstrip(\"/\")\n        if not url.endswith(\"/chat/completions\"):\n            if url.endswith(\"/v1\"):\n                url = f\"{url}/chat/completions\"\n            else:\n                url = f\"{url}/v1/chat/completions\"\n                \n        api_key = getattr(self.config, 'local_api_key', '[REDACTED_CREDENTIAL]')\n        \n        try:\n            response = http_requests.post(\n                url,\n                headers={\n                    \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {api_key}\",\n                    \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n                },\n                json=body,\n                timeout=(30, 300),\n            )\n        except Exception as conn_err:\n            self._log_provider_error(url, model, inputs, str(conn_err), \"NETWORK_CONNECTION_FAILED\")\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"Connection to local LLM failed ({url}): {conn_err}\")\n\n        if response.status_code != 200:\n            err_msg = f\"HTTP {response.status_code}: {response.text[:300]}\"\n            self._log_provider_error(url, model, inputs, response.text, f\"HTTP_{response.status_code}\")\n            raise RuntimeError(err_msg)\n\n        try:\n            resp_json = response.json()\n        except Exception as e:\n            self._log_provider_error(url, model, inputs, response.text, \"INVALID_HTTP_JSON\")\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"Local API did not return valid HTTP JSON: {response.text[:300]}\")\n\n        choices = resp_json.get(\"choices\")\n        if not choices or not isinstance(choices, list):\n            self._log_provider_error(url, model, inputs, response.text, \"EMPTY_CHOICES\")\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"Local API returned no choices: {response.text[:300]}\")\n\n        content = choices[0].get(\"message\", {}).get(\"content\", \"\")\n        if not isinstance(content, str):\n            content = str(content or \"\")\n\n        # Check if MSEMAX returned an error string inside content\n        if content.strip().startswith(\"[Error:\"):\n            self._log_provider_error(url, model, inputs, content, \"MSEMAX_ERROR_STRING\")\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"MSEMAX Error: {content.strip()}\")\n\n        # Robust JSON extraction\n        clean = content.strip()\n        # 1. Try markdown code block extraction\n        md_match = re.search(r\"```(?:json)?\\s*(\\{.*\\}|\\[.*\\])\\s*```\", clean, re.DOTALL)\n        if md_match:\n            clean = md_match.group(1).strip()\n        else:\n            # 2. Try outermost curly braces\n            curly_match = re.search(r'\\{.*\\}', clean, re.DOTALL)\n            if curly_match:\n                clean = curly_match.group(0).strip()\n            else:\n                # 3. Try outermost square brackets\n                bracket_match = re.search(r'\\[.*\\]', clean, re.DOTALL)\n                if bracket_match:\n                    clean = bracket_match.group(0).strip()\n\n        try:\n            answer = json.loads(clean)\n        except json.JSONDecodeError as jde:\n            self._log_provider_error(url, model, inputs, content, f\"JSON_DECODE_ERROR: {jde}\")\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"JSON Parse Error ({jde}): Model output was: {content[:300]}\")\n\n        # If answer is a list of results directly\n        if isinstance(answer, list):\n            results = answer\n        elif isinstance(answer, dict):\n            results = answer.get(\"results\", [])\n        else:\n            results = []\n\n        # Map by case_id\n        decision_map = {d.get(\"case_id\"): d for d in results if isinstance(d, dict)}\n\n        return [decision_map.get(c[\"case_id\"], {\"status\": \"no_match\", \"item_id\": \"\"}) for c in inputs[\"cases\"]]\n\n    def _log_provider_error(self, url: str, model: str, inputs: dict, raw_response: str, error_type: str):\n        try:\n            from datetime import datetime\n            import os\n            log_dir = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(__file__))), \"data\")\n            os.makedirs(log_dir, exist_ok=True)\n            log_file = os.path.join(log_dir, \"provider_errors.log\")\n            \n            case_ids = [c.get(\"case_id\") for c in inputs.get(\"cases\", [])]\n            entry = (\n                f\"\\n{'='*70}\\n\"\n                f\"TIMESTAMP: {datetime.now().isoformat()}\\n\"\n                f\"ERROR TYPE: {error_type}\\n\"\n                f\"URL: {url} | MODEL: {model}\\n\"\n                f\"CASE COUNT: {len(case_ids)} | CASES: {case_ids}\\n\"\n                f\"RAW RESPONSE:\\n{raw_response}\\n\"\n                f\"{'='*70}\\n\"\n            )\n            with open(log_file, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n                f.write(entry)\n        except Exception as log_err:\n            print(f\"[!] Warning: Failed to write to provider_errors.log: {log_err}\")\n","StartLine":533,"TargetContent":"    def _call_local_api(self, inputs: dict) -> list[dict]:\n        model = getattr(self.config, 'local_model', 'gpt-4o')\n        \n        body = {\n            \"model\": model,\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": SYSTEM_PROMPT},\n                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": json.dumps(inputs, ensure_ascii=False)}\n            ]\n        }\n\n        raw_url = getattr(self.config, 'local_api_url', \"http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1/chat/completions\")\n        url = str(raw_url).strip().rstrip(\"/\")\n        if not url.endswith(\"/chat/completions\"):\n            if url.endswith(\"/v1\"):\n                url = f\"{url}/chat/completions\"\n            else:\n                url = f\"{url}/v1/chat/completions\"\n                \n        api_key = getattr(self.config, 'local_api_key', '[REDACTED_CREDENTIAL]')\n        \n        response = http_requests.post(\n            url,\n            headers={\n                \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {api_key}\",\n                \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n            },\n            json=body,\n            timeout=(30, 300),\n        )\n\n        if response.status_code != 200:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"HTTP {response.status_code}: {response.text[:200]}\")\n\n        resp_json = response.json()\n        content = resp_json[\"choices\"][0][\"message\"][\"content\"]\n        \n        # Check if MSEMAX returned an error string inside content\n        if content.strip().startswith(\"[Error:\"):\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"MSEMAX Error: {content.strip()}\")\n            \n        # Clean markdown wrappers if any\n        clean = content.strip()\n        if \"```\" in clean:\n            clean = re.sub(r\"^```(?:json)?\\s*\", \"\", clean, flags=re.MULTILINE)\n            clean = re.sub(r\"```\\s*$\", \"\", clean, flags=re.MULTILINE)\n            clean = clean.strip()\n            \n        json_match = re.search(r'\\{.*\\}', clean, re.DOTALL)\n        if json_match:\n            clean = json_match.group(0)\n            \n        try:\n            answer = json.loads(clean)\n        except json.JSONDecodeError as jde:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"JSON Parse Error ({jde}): Model output was: {clean[:300]}\")\n            \n        results = answer.get(\"results\", [])\n        \n        # Map by case_id\n        decision_map = {d.get(\"case_id\"): d for d in results}\n        \n        return [decision_map.get(c[\"case_id\"], {\"status\": \"no_match\", \"item_id\": \"\"}) for c in inputs[\"cases\"]]","TargetFile":"D:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\src\\fast_match\\coordinator.py","toolAction":"Updating _call_local_api","toolSummary":"Replace _call_local_api in coordinator.py"}}]}
